+# Production Enable Playbook (detailed)
+
+This playbook enumerates steps, checks and required signoffs before enabling automated promotions and enabling speculative decoding beyond canary.
+
+1) Prechecks (Operators)
+ - Cosign & KMS: ensure cosign-kms secret exists and that CI can sign artifacts (verify by running cosign_signing.yml).
+ - TLS for admission: generate webhook TLS via cert-manager; verify ValidatingWebhookConfiguration in place.
+ - Argo/Tekton: workflows & service accounts installed and tested in ml-pipelines namespace.
+ - Model registry: verify candidate artifacts are uploaded and accessible and that Object Lock is enabled for evidence bucket.
+
+2) Verifier & Safety
+ - Run finetune with domain manifest (services/factuality/finetune_domain.py).
+ - Run adversarial tests: services/ci/adversarial_suite.py and fairness: services/ci/fairness_check.py.
+ - SME signoff: request SME via services/factuality/sme_signoff.py; at least one approve required for auto‑promotion.
+
+3) Canary & Shadow
+ - Run Argo workflow training-validation-promotion in dry-run to ensure no unexpected failures.
+ - Shadow for at least 7 days and validate metrics (acceptance_rate, verifier precision).
+ - If stable, run canary (1% → 5%); only enable auto-promote after at least 72h stable canary and SME signoff.
+
+4) RL & Policy actions
+ - RL actions must be requested via safe RL agent and require manual approval before application.
+ - Only after 90 days of stable offline evaluation and low safety risk may operator consider limited automation for low-risk changes.
+
+5) Sustainability & Kernel
+ - Run wattmeter calibration and validate telemetry calibration values in Grafana.
+ - Run kernel autotuner CI on representative GPU hosts and validate results with services/triton/kernel_opt/validate_kernel_results.py.
+
+Signoffs required from: SRE, ML Lead, Security, Compliance, Product SME.
+
